ion and lens cell age</article-title><source>J Gerontol</source><year>1983</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>287</fpage><lpage>292</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6841922</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lens cytoplasmic phase separation</article-title><source>Int Rev Cytol</source><year>2000</year><volume>192</volume><fpage>171</fpage><lpage>187</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10553279</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bettelheim</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Maisel H</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Physical basis of lens transparency</article-title><source>The Ocular Lens: Structure, Function and Pathology</source><year>1985</year><publisher-name>New York and Basel, Marcel Dekker, Inc.</publisher-name><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>300</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Al Ghoul</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Costello</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fiber cell morphology and cytoplasmic texture in cataractous and normal human lens nuclei</article-title><source>Curr Eye Res</source><year>1996</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>542</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8670754</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3109/02713689609000764</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Al-Ghoul</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Costello</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Light microscopic variation of fiber cell size, shape and ordering in the equatorial plane of bovine and human lenses.</article-title><source>Molecular Vision</source><year>1997</year><volume>3</volume><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9238091</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Al-Ghoul</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nordgren</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuszak</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Freel</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Costello</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuszak</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structural evidence of nuclear fiber compaction as a function of aging and cataractogenesis.</article-title><source>Exper Eye Res</source><year>2001</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>214</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11180969</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/exer.2000.0937</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freel</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Ghoul</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuszak</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Costello</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of nuclear fiber cell compaction in transparent and cataractous diabetic human lenses by scanning electron microscopy</article-title><source>BMC Ophthalmol</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>1</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12515578</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2415-3-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown<